106
00:07:56.415 --> 00:07:57.289
Part 2.

107
00:07:57.569 --> 00:07:59.447
Core Concepts, Beginner to Deep.

108
00:08:00.697 --> 00:08:02.659
Intuition: a shop's cash book.

109
00:08:02.939 --> 00:08:05.627
A shopkeeper writes every movement of money twice:

110
00:08:05.907 --> 00:08:09.278
240 rupeesinto the till, from Ravi's order.

111
00:08:09.558 --> 00:08:13.121
Nothing is erased; mistakes are fixed by writing a new line.

112
00:08:13.401 --> 00:08:16.771
At closing time, the till is counted and must match the book.

113
00:08:17.051 --> 00:08:21.062
The bank statement arrives the next day and is ticked off line by line.

114
00:08:21.342 --> 00:08:30.110
A payment system is that book, kept by computers that sometimes hear the same thing twice, sometimes not at all, and sometimes from someone lying.

115
00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:32.420
Requirements.

116
00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:33.553
Functional.

117
00:08:33.833 --> 00:08:42.601
Accept payments by UPI (intent, collect), cards (tokenised), netbanking and wallets through one or more gateways; cash on delivery.

118
00:08:42.881 --> 00:08:45.953
Full and partial refunds, to source or to wallet.

119
00:08:46.233 --> 00:08:49.433
A customer wallet with cashback, refunds and payments.

120
00:08:49.713 --> 00:08:55.473
Payment status for checkout and support; receipts and GST invoices (Ch 36).

121
00:08:55.753 --> 00:08:59.017
Daily reconciliation with settlements; vendor payouts.

122
00:09:00.367 --> 00:09:01.477
Non-functional.

123
00:09:01.757 --> 00:09:09.479
Correctness: never charge twice for one order, never fulfil unpaid, never lose a captured payment; ledger always balanced.

124
00:09:09.759 --> 00:09:18.933
Availability: payments during peaks (festival sales) at 99.95%; graceful degradation (COD, other methods).

125
00:09:19.213 --> 00:09:25.357
Latency: checkout creation 300 ms; status within seconds of the gateway's decision.

126
00:09:25.637 --> 00:09:37.391
Security and compliance: no raw card data (PCI DSS scope minimised), RBI tokenisation and payment-data storage in India, audit trails, data retention.

127
00:09:38.741 --> 00:09:39.787
Estimation.

128
00:09:40.067 --> 00:09:41.411
Here is a quick table:

129
00:09:41.691 --> 00:09:43.120
Quantity, and Estimate.

130
00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:50.483
Orders: ~1.5M per day; peak ~100 payments per second, 5 to 10x during sales.

131
00:09:50.763 --> 00:09:51.595
Methods:

132
00:09:51.875 --> 00:09:58.019
UPI ~70%, cards ~20%, others ~10% (illustrative).

133
00:09:58.299 --> 00:10:03.419
Webhooks: ~2 to 3 events per payment, then ~300 per second peak.

134
00:10:03.699 --> 00:10:12.723
Ledger: ~4 legs per payment (capture, fee, settlement, refunds), then ~6M legs per day; append-only, partitioned by month.

135
00:10:13.003 --> 00:10:18.293
Reconciliation: ~1.5M settlement rows per day matched in a batch.

136
00:10:19.643 --> 00:10:21.969
The volumes are modest for a database.

137
00:10:22.249 --> 00:10:26.707
The difficulty is correctness under unreliable messages, not throughput.

138
00:10:28.057 --> 00:10:30.447
The ledger: double-entry, append-only.

139
00:10:30.727 --> 00:10:41.564
Accounts: customer wallets, pspclearing (money the gateway owes us), bank (our account), merchantpayable, feesexpense, refundspayable, vendor payables, tax liabilities.

140
00:10:41.844 --> 00:10:50.697
Entries: every business event (capture, refund, settlement, fee, cashback) is one entry with two or more legs whose amounts sum to zero.

141
00:10:50.977 --> 00:11:02.156
A capture of 500 rupeesdebits pspclearing and credits revenue or merchantpayable; the next day's settlement debits bank and feesexpense and credits pspclearing.

142
00:11:02.436 --> 00:11:08.132
Immutability: entries are never updated or deleted; corrections are reversing entries.

143
00:11:08.412 --> 00:11:10.183
The ledger is the audit trail.

144
00:11:11.533 --> 00:11:17.101
Balances are projections: the sum of legs, cached per account and maintained transactionally.

145
00:11:17.381 --> 00:11:22.693
Money types: integer minor units (paise), never floating point; currency per account.

146
