175
00:12:24.323 --> 00:12:28.248
Every movement (58,764 retries).

176
00:12:29.598 --> 00:12:37.918
Lost updates are the classic money bug: two operations read the same balance and each writes its own result (Ch 05).

177
00:12:38.198 --> 00:12:49.462
SERIALIZABLE gives correct results with no application locking, but hot accounts (busy wallets, the platform's clearing account) turn conflict detection into retry storms.

178
00:12:49.742 --> 00:12:51.769
Use it for low-contention invariants.

179
00:12:53.119 --> 00:12:59.369
The production shape: append-only balanced legs + a balance row per account, updated under SELECT...

180
00:12:59.649 --> 00:13:06.028
FOR UPDATE in the same transaction, with a CHECK (balance = 0) for accounts that can't go negative.

181
00:13:06.308 --> 00:13:13.327
For very hot internal accounts (clearing), aggregate legs asynchronously or shard the account into sub-accounts.

182
00:13:14.677 --> 00:13:16.042
The payment state machine.

183
00:13:16.322 --> 00:13:17.239
On screen:

184
00:13:17.519 --> 00:13:21.210
CREATED ──(authorised)──► AUTHORISED ──(captured)──► CAPTURED ──(refund)──►.

185
00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:27.570
PARTIALLYREFUNDED or REFUNDED. │ ▲. └──(failed)──► FAILED ──(later attempt captured)──────┘ CREATED ──(expired)──►.

186
00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:28.767
EXPIRED.

187
00:13:31.617 --> 00:13:37.911
Create a payment row with our id and an idempotency key (per checkout attempt) before calling the gateway.

188
00:13:38.191 --> 00:13:44.463
Create the gateway order with our id as its receipt or reference, so the gateway itself dedupes retries.

189
00:13:44.743 --> 00:13:47.004
Transitions are guarded in the database:

190
00:13:47.284 --> 00:13:50.847
UPDATE payments SET status='CAPTURED' WHERE id=?

191
00:13:51.127 --> 00:13:53.623
AND status IN ('CREATED','AUTHORISED','FAILED').

192
00:13:53.903 --> 00:13:55.524
Exactly one caller wins.

193
00:13:55.804 --> 00:14:02.929
Fulfilment is triggered only by the transition into CAPTURED (an outbox event), never by the arrival of a message.

194
00:14:04.279 --> 00:14:12.194
Webhooks are the authoritative push signal: verify the signature, dedupe by event id, process at-least-once and out of order.

195
00:14:12.474 --> 00:14:16.122
A late failed for an earlier attempt must not overwrite a capture.

196
00:14:16.402 --> 00:14:19.623
The client callback (checkout success) is a UI hint.

197
00:14:19.903 --> 00:14:24.362
It triggers a status check against the gateway, never a state change by itself.

198
00:14:24.642 --> 00:14:38.402
Unknown outcomes (timeouts, missing webhooks): poll the gateway's status API for anything non-terminal past a threshold, and let daily reconciliation be the final authority (Ch 13 NEEDSATTENTION).

