406
00:26:23.731 --> 00:26:38.941
Context, Double fulfilment from app callback + webhook; charged-without-order from lost webhooks; tampered success callbacks; wallet drift from mutable balances; unexplained settlement gaps; gateway-level failover during a bank outage.

407
00:26:40.291 --> 00:27:02.179
Decision, Guarded payment state machine driven by verified webhooks and status polling; double-entry append-only ledger with locked balance projections; end-to-end idempotency keys; daily three-way reconciliation with rules and exception queue; routing by health per (gateway, method, bank) with customer steering and PSP-side auto-retry.

408
00:27:03.529 --> 00:27:11.423
Related ADRs, ADR-310 Ledger: entries + legs, integer paise, balance rows under FOR UPDATE,

409
00:27:11.703 --> 00:27:33.740
CHECK non-negative wallets (L1); ADR-311 Payment state machine with guarded UPDATEs; webhook signature + event dedupe; app callback is a hint (L2); ADR-312 Status poller for CREATED or AUTHORISED or FAILED older than 2 min within the payment window (L2); ADR-313 Reconciliation:

410
00:27:34.020 --> 00:28:00.452
T+3 carry-forward, ±1 paisa, fee rules per method, duplicate detection, three-way with bank UTRs (L3); ADR-314 Routing per (gateway, method, bank), 85% threshold, 5% probe, steer customers on bank-side outages, one auto-retry for PSP-side errors (L4); ADR-315 Hosted checkout and tokenisation only; no card data in our systems.

411
00:28:01.802 --> 00:28:02.762
Requirements.

412
00:28:03.042 --> 00:28:08.077
R1 Zero double charges per order and zero fulfilment without capture.

413
00:28:08.357 --> 00:28:15.973
R2 Every captured payment either fulfilled or refunded within 30 minutes (poller) and within 1 day (reconciliation).

414
00:28:16.253 --> 00:28:21.437
R3 Ledger balanced at all times; wallet balances equal the sum of their legs.

415
00:28:21.717 --> 00:28:27.434
R4 Reconciliation exceptions triaged within 1 business day, each with rupee impact.

416
00:28:27.714 --> 00:28:36.631
R5 Payment success ≥ 95% excluding customer-side failures, including during single-gateway incidents.

417
00:28:37.981 --> 00:28:39.389
Decisions in detail.

418
00:28:39.669 --> 00:28:58.315
Ledger (ADR-310). entries(id, kind, ref, createdat), legs(entryid, account, amount), accountbalances(account, balance, version); monthly partitions; nightly invariant job (sum of legs = 0 per entry; balance = sum of legs per account).

419
00:28:58.595 --> 00:29:02.669
State machine (ADR-311 or 312).

420
00:29:02.949 --> 00:29:10.971
Transitions only via one stored procedure per event type; outbox rows in the same transaction; poller every 30 s.

421
00:29:11.251 --> 00:29:14.301
Reconciliation (ADR-313).

422
00:29:14.581 --> 00:29:23.861
Settlement files ingested on arrival; matching engine with rules as configuration; exceptions to a finance queue with categories and owners.

423
00:29:25.211 --> 00:29:27.665
Routing (ADR-314).

424
00:29:27.945 --> 00:29:33.619
Health from success rates and error-code classes per (gateway, method, bank) over 5 minutes.

425
00:29:33.899 --> 00:29:36.502
Security (ADR-315).

426
00:29:36.782 --> 00:29:42.926
Webhook HMAC with rotated secrets; refund approvals above 10,000 rupees; audit log.

427
00:29:43.206 --> 00:29:44.230
Consequences.

428
00:29:44.510 --> 00:29:51.486
More moving parts (poller, reconciliation, router) and dependence on gateway APIs and file formats.

429
00:29:51.766 --> 00:29:54.326
Status sometimes lags by seconds to minutes.

430
00:29:54.606 --> 00:30:02.457
In return: no double shipments, no unpaid orders, a ledger that balances, and a daily proof that the money is where the books say.

